AITM_DELIVERY_RESULT: {"action":null,"branchDisposition":"retained","intent":{"attributionTokens":["#1562"],"baseRef":"trunk","clientCreatedAt":"2026-09-10T04:57:47.000Z","commitMessage":"* [#1562] feat(delivery): add merge-method reconciliation lane\n\nA delivery intent's merge method could only ever come from configuration\n(fullAutoMerge.mergeMethod), so a pull request merged with a different method\nstranded its issue: delivery-verification refused the mismatch, close demanded\na receipt, and no flag reached the condition. Observed on #680, whose PR #1556\nwas merged from the GitHub UI as a merge commit against a squash-only config.\n\nThe verifier is deliberately unchanged. What was wrong is that only config\ncould state the intent; the lane lets an operator restate it to the OBSERVED\nmethod, then the existing equality check verifies that restatement.\n\nThe lane cannot launder a false receipt:\n\n- resolveReconciledMergeMethod accepts a declared method only when live\n  topology agrees; declaring squash for a two-parent merge still refuses\n- a no-op reconciliation matching configuration refuses\n- observeMergeMethod refuses an unattributable single-parent rewrite rather\n  than guessing squash\n- a placeholder-rejected reason is mandatory and recorded\n\nThe divergence is its own append-only record rather than a field on the intent\nor receipt, whose v1 schemas are pinned behind strict exact-key validation.\n\nclose's refusal now names the lane, so --force stops being the only\ndiscoverable escape.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [#1562] refactor(close): extract and pin the delivery-gate refusal message\n\nThe refusal now names the merge-method reconciliation lane, so an operator who\nhits close-delivery-receipt:missing learns the route out from the message\nrather than from the source. Extracted to a module-scope buildDeliveryGateRefusal\nso a test can pin the guidance.\n\nThe test also asserts the message never advertises --force: that flag does not\nreach refuseDeliveryGate, and suggesting it would send an operator down the same\ndead end that stranded #680.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [#1562] test(fixtures): record the package and emitter surface changes\n\nTwo hand-maintained baselines move because this change ships real code, and\nboth are meant to make such moves review-visible rather than to forbid them.\n\npackage-boundary: the reconciliation record is one shipped runtime module, so\nthe exact packed surface grows by one. Ceiling 774 -> 775, annotated in the same\nform as every prior bump.\n\ntiming-event-emitter characterization: close.mjs emitter call sites shift up by\nthree lines. buildDeliveryGateRefusal is deliberately appended at the END of\nclose.mjs — inserting it near the top shifted every characterized line by twelve\nand turned an unrelated change into fixture churn. The residual three-line shift\ncomes from collapsing the inline refusal string into a single call, which is the\npoint of the extraction.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* [#1562] fix(fixtures): commit the post-merge emitter line numbers\n\nThe merge commit cf5aa095 shipped trunk's stale close.mjs emitter line numbers\n(2480, 2678, 2823, 3057) instead of the corrected post-merge positions. The\ncorrection was made and verified in the working tree but never reached the\nindex, so the pushed branch failed the characterization test it was reported\nas passing.\n\nCorrects to the actual merged positions: 2477, 2675, 2820, 3054 — trunk's\nvalues minus the three lines this branch removes by collapsing the inline\ndelivery-gate refusal into a single call.\n\nVerified against HEAD after committing this time, not against the working tree.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","commitMessageSha256":"6fcdd81098b4e5d3ebecfa77c81a4a754eb36495c1bfd2afa95df42857374675","commitTitle":"[#1562] feat(delivery): merge-method reconciliation lane (#1571)","commitTitleSha256":"e302e24e5e3ae7ecbcbb67e9c9daf15ec0e2cc3fd7b199b13c33354a2449ca74","expectedHeadSha":"f0a11c21261a846a9f424fd15f66aedb0f89ed88","headRef":"claude/1562-merge-method-reconcile","intentId":"01M24TWVAKRWEHANK4B2BYJ0BH","issueNumber":1562,"mergeMethod":"squash","prNumber":1571,"provider":"external","repository":"kburson/ai-task-manager","schema":"aitm.delivery-intent/v1","sessionId":"514e69c4-8a9e-401a-ac82-3f46009139ed","state":"pending","supersedesIntentId":null},"mode":"current-head","receipt":{"baseRef":"trunk","expectedHeadSha":"f0a11c21261a846a9f424fd15f66aedb0f89ed88","intentId":"01M24TWVAKRWEHANK4B2BYJ0BH","issueNumber":1562,"mergeCommitSha":"8fed51cf10230fd6ed6709cabbb27c80a69b9d14","mergeMethod":"squash","prNumber":1571,"provider":"external","result":"delivered","schema":"aitm.delivery-receipt/v1","sessionId":"514e69c4-8a9e-401a-ac82-3f46009139ed","verifiedAt":"2026-09-10T04:57:47.000Z","verifiedTrunkRef":"origin/trunk"},"recovery":true,"status":"delivered"}
